WEBVTT

00:02:29.822 --> 00:02:33.175
and I don't recall once in his 40 years
of chemical engineering

00:02:33.199 --> 00:02:36.857
anybody asking him if he was afraid
to be a chemical engineer, you know?

00:02:36.881 --> 00:02:42.668
"That chemical-engineering block,
John, how's it going?"

00:02:42.692 --> 00:02:44.832
It just didn't come up
like that, you know?

00:02:44.856 --> 00:02:48.666
But to be fair,
chemical engineers as a group

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:51.214
haven't really earned
a reputation over the centuries

00:02:51.238 --> 00:02:53.910
for being alcoholic manic-depressives.

00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:55.358
(Laughter)

00:02:55.382 --> 00:02:58.192
We writers, we kind of do have
that reputation,

00:02:58.216 --> 00:03:02.175
and not just writers,
but creative people across all genres,